AutoPagerize integration notice
================================

This directory contains an integration derived from AutoPagerize 0.3.9:

  Project: http://autopagerize.net/
  Source:  https://github.com/swdyh/autopagerize
  Author:  swdyh
  License: GPL (core user script) + MIT (extension abstraction layer)

The complete GPL and MIT texts are retained in LICENSE beside this notice.

Modified for formant on 2026-08-12:

* The upstream MV2 background page, page_action, chrome.extension.connect
  port messaging, and localStorage caching are replaced with an MV3
  service-worker bridge and chrome.storage.
* The wedata.net auto-update fetch is removed; the bundled siteinfo.json
  (converted from the upstream JSONP payload to plain JSON) is the primary
  site-rule source, with a small high-priority builtin override list for
  modern Google / Bing search DOM. Users may add custom rules via the
  option panel.
* Same-origin next-page fetches run in the content script (to keep the
  tab's cookies / consent); only cross-origin pages use the service-worker
  fetch bridge.
* The cross-browser abstraction (Safari/Firefox/Greasemonkey branches) is
  removed; only the Chrome MV3 content-script path is retained.
* The loading/error message bar is rebuilt as a Shadow DOM element to
  avoid leaking styles into the host page.
* The core XPath, scroll-detection, next-page loading, and DOM insertion
  logic is preserved from the upstream autopagerize.user.js under GPL.

formant is distributed under GPLv3 (due to the V2EX Plus integration).
The GPL-licensed AutoPagerize core is compatible with that distribution.
